integ5 0069 = patches/pdl5/0067-glm-pdl-reduce.patch (overnight 2026-10-31), renumbered for the integrated stack on 3f94715d.

pdl5 0067: glm_mm_reduce waits for its matmul and launches as its dependent (TF_GLM_PDL_CHAIN).
- glm_mm.cu: glm_mm_reduce calls griddepcontrol.wait (qmm_frag::grid_wait) right after its existing trigger, before it
  reads part, writes out or exits; native sm_120 SASS: ACQBULK at instr 7, nothing but PREEXIT before it.
- cuda_mm.zig: Chain {reduce, hc, p2p} from TF_GLM_PDL_CHAIN (unset or 1: all, 0: none, or a comma list; TF_GLM_PDL=0
  turns it off with glm_mm's own PDL); mm.Kernels.chain; the K-slice reduce launches with .pdl = chain.reduce.
- cuda_moe.zig: the shared expert's side stream gets a copy of the kernels with no chain (side stream excluded).
- glm_mm_policy_host.zig: the reduce's attribute follows chain.reduce at 1/8/32 rows; Chain.parse's values.
Exact by construction: same kernels, same arithmetic; every access to another grid's data after the wait.

